<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">VEF</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1919</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Valsts Elektrotehniskā Fabrika</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">VEF (Valsts Elektrotehniskā Fabrika, State Electrotechnical Factory) was a state-owned electrical manufacturer in Riga, established in 1919. In the 1930s it became known for radios, telephones, light aircraft and, from 1938, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minox">Minox</a> miniature camera. Under Soviet rule it was a major producer of telephone equipment and radios, and it declined after the restoration of independence in 1991.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vef.jpg" alt="VEF" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mārtiņš Bruņenieks · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:VEF_p%C4%81rvaldes_%C4%93ka_p%C4%93c_restaur%C4%81cijas_2017.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
